.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt BSD3-SESSION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsd3-session
.Nd register and supervise an ordinary local Wayland session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
requires an ordinary user in the foreground process group of a real controlling
FreeBSD virtual terminal.
It opens a ConsoleKit session or validates an inherited cookie against the
caller's PID, UID, local Wayland/user identity, actual VT and active state.
The runtime directory must belong to the caller with mode0700.
Failure prevents execution of the command; cookies are never printed.
.Pp
The original registration connection stays open while the child runs.
The child retains its controlling terminal on standard input.
Native procctl descendant supervision forwards termination and reaps remaining
session processes, including processes that detach into another session.
Termination escalates after five seconds; final cleanup is bounded.
A newly created session is closed on exit; an inherited session is not closed.
Loss of the pinned ConsoleKit owner terminates the command.
This cannot recover a frozen kernel or signal a child that acquired different
privileges through an unrelated privileged program.
.Pp
The opt-in
.Pa libexec/bsd3-sddm-session
adapter runs this launcher, a private session D-Bus and SDDM's existing Wayland
profile script.
An example SDDM fragment is installed under
.Pa share/examples/bsd-cubed/sddm-wayland.conf .
Installation does not enable it, modify PAM or replace a desktop entry.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The child's exit status is returned after cleanup.
Setup or cleanup failure returns nonzero.
Root and invalid invocation are refused.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bsddd 8 ,
.Xr bsd3-vt-guard 8 ,
.Xr procctl 2
